   deleting the older log files : find , mtime

   find command is used to find the file in a directory
   find . -name '*.log' : it will find all the files with extension .log in the current directory
 it supports seaching the file by name , owner , modification time,date,size,etc

   find . -mtime -2 : it will find all the files which are modified in last 2 days
   +2 means more than 2 days
   -2 means less than 2 days
   2 exactly 2 days
   find . -type f : it will find all the files in the current directory
   find . -type d : it will find all the directories in the current directory
   find . -type l : it will find all the symbolic links in the current directory

   #=================================================================== sed ==========================
   cat editor.txt == sed -n 'p' editor.txt 
   sed -n '5,10p' editor.txt # to print line from 5 to 10
   sed  '10d' editor.txt # to print without the 10th line
   # if you want to actually delete from the file then make use of -i
   sed -i '5,10d' editor.txt 
   # befor deleting if you want to take the backup of the file then delete in the original file
   sed -i.back '2d' editor.txt

            #============= finding abd replacing the content ===========================#
   sed 's/Line/line/' editor.txt   # it only takes the first occurance of each line
   sed 's/Line/line/g' editor.txt   # it changes all the occurances 
   # if you want to change only one line  which starts in the word games in the file by replacing  usr to user
   sed '/games/s/usr/user/' editor.txt
               
